# ## Golden dev-image version pins (single source of truth)
#
# Sourced by:
#   - scripts/build-dev-image.sh (converts every KEY into a --build-arg)
#   - images/dev/Dockerfile      (declares a matching ARG for every KEY below)
#
# Format: KEY=value (no spaces around =, no quotes). BASH-sourceable, so this
# file must stay parseable by `set -a; . file; set +a`.
#
# Naming contract between the two files: each KEY here is also an ARG in the
# Dockerfile. The build script refuses to continue if an ARG is missing from the
# Dockerfile (a typo would otherwise silently build with the Dockerfile default),
# and Dockerfile ARG defaults are mirrored from here so `docker build` works
# standalone too.
#
# Unqualified entries were VERIFIED against upstream on 2026-09-27 (asset URL
# returned HTTP 200/206, or the package/version exists on the registry).
# Entries marked `UNVERIFIED` could not be confirmed to exist upstream — see the
# note on each line.

# ── Base OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pinned to the Ubuntu 24.04 LTS "noble" tag. Tagged deliberately rather than
# relying on `ubuntu:latest`, which is how the repo's old codercom/example-base
# silently re-based itself under us.
UBUNTU_VERSION=24.04

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Installed side-by-side from nodejs.org tarballs into /opt/node/<major>, not
# from NodeSource: both node_22.x and node_24.x apt repos ship a package called
# `nodejs`, so the second one would replace the first.
# cyborg-conductor-core and dgx-spark-it-up pin Node 24; nvidia-dgx-spark-lab
# dashboard requires engines.node >=22. Node 24 is the default; Node 22 is
# selectable with `NODE_VERSION=22` (see the Dockerfile ENV comment).
NODE_VERSION_DEFAULT=24
NODE_22_VERSION=22.23.3
NODE_24_VERSION=24.21.0
# Matches nvidia-dgx-spark-lab tool-versions.env PRETTIER_VERSION (3.9.4).
# npm `latest` has since moved to 3.9.9; staying on the repo's pin keeps
# `//:lints:yaml_format` output byte-identical with that repo.
PRETTIER_VERSION=3.9.4

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3.12 is the noble default; 3.11 comes from the deadsnakes PPA (noble is a
# supported suite there) because noble's own archive has no python3.11.
PYTHON_DEFAULT_VERSION=3.12
PYTHON_311_VERSION=3.11
# Official standalone installer (astral-sh/uv). Pinned so the installer URL is
# reproducible; the script also ships a checksum-verified path.
UV_VERSION=0.12.19
# `uv tool install` args for ruff/mypy are versioned here so a lint-rule bump is
# a one-line edit. ruff/mypy `latest` at pin time: 0.16.9 / 2.3.1.
RUFF_VERSION=0.16.9
MYPY_VERSION=2.3.1

# ── Offline MCP servers (pre-cached so a workspace needs no network) ─────────
# All four names VERIFIED to exist:
#   npm:  @modelcontextprotocol/server-{filesystem,memory,sequential-thinking}
#   PyPI: mcp-server-git, mcp-server-time
# The three npm servers move in lockstep on CalVer; 2026.8.31 is the current
# published tag for all three.
MCP_NODE_SERVERS_VERSION=2026.8.31
# PyPI releases for both Python servers: 2026.8.18 (current at pin time).
MCP_PY_SERVERS_VERSION=2026.8.18

# ── Go toolchain ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Go 1.24 required (ProtoMCP declares go 1.22.3, so 1.24 satisfies it).
# Latest 1.24.x patch at pin time. Official tarball into /usr/local/go — the
# golang-1.24 apt package drops binaries in /usr/lib/go-1.24/bin, which breaks
# every "export PATH=$PATH:/usr/local/go/bin" snippet in the wild.
GO_VERSION=1.24.13
# Go plugin binaries are pinned by package-path@version so `go install` is
# reproducible; `@latest` would bake a different protoc-gen-go on every rebuild.
# The `@version` MUST be the suffix of the full package path — `go install`
# rejects `module@version/cmd/tool` as a disallowed version string, which is what
# the first build of this layer hit. VERIFIED: all three resolve on
# proxy.golang.org and build with Go 1.24 (see the Go layer comment in the
# Dockerfile).
# The newest release of each needs a newer Go, so these are NOT simply "latest":
#   protoc-gen-go-grpc v1.6.2 -> go 1.25.0   (pinned v1.6.1 -> 1.24.0)
#   x/tools        v0.50.0    -> go 1.26.0   (pinned v0.40.0 -> 1.24.0)
# Bump GO_VERSION together with these three.
PROTOBUF_GO_MODULE=google.golang.org/protobuf/cmd/protoc-gen-go@v1.36.12
PROTOC_GEN_GO_GRPC_MODULE=google.golang.org/grpc/cmd/protoc-gen-go-grpc@v1.6.1
STRINGER_MODULE=golang.org/x/tools/cmd/stringer@v0.40.0

# ── protobuf ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# protoc from the official release zip. VERIFIED asset:
# protoc-36.2-linux-x86_64.zip
PROTOC_VERSION=36.2

# ── Terraform toolchain (templates/docker-dev + inkorporated) ────────────────
TERRAFORM_VERSION=1.16.4
# tflint is published under terraform-linters/tflint. The aquasecurity/tflint
# repo 404s — it was renamed upstream. Keep this bare: the Dockerfile adds the
# leading "v" that GitHub's tag carries. First build proved it — without the
# prefix the fetch 404s and the layer aborts.
TFLINT_VERSION=0.64.0
# terragrunt tags kept the leading "v" through the 1.x line (checked against the
# GitHub release API: v1.1.6 serves terragrunt_linux_amd64), so the Dockerfile
# prefixes this value in the URL. Keep it bare.
TERRAGRUNT_VERSION=1.1.6
# VERIFIED asset: gh_2.101.0_linux_amd64.tar.gz. Pinned rather than apt because
# noble's gh is 2.45 and predates several `gh` subcommands the agent experience
# (and scripts/bootstrap.sh's successors) rely on.
GH_VERSION=2.101.0

# ── Coder CLI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Matches the coder server image tag in docker-compose.yml
# (ghcr.io/coder/coder:v2.36.6). The CLI and server versions must agree or
# `coder template push` produces a provisioner/agent skew.
CODER_CLI_VERSION=v2.36.6

# ── Pins inherited from toxicoder/nvidia-dgx-spark-lab ───────────────────────
# Read from .devcontainer/tool-versions.env on 2026-09-27 and copied verbatim so
# this image builds the same Bazel/k8s toolchain that repo's //:lint expects.
# All six asset URLs VERIFIED (HTTP 206 on a ranged GET).
BAZELISK_VERSION=v1.25.0
BUILDIFIER_VERSION=v8.2.1
SHFMT_ASSET_VERSION=3.10.0
KUBECONFORM_VERSION=v0.8.0
HELM_VERSION=v3.15.0
# Upstream calls this KUBECTL_VERSION in nvidia-dgx-spark-lab; the name below is
# what the Dockerfile ARG uses. Same value, renamed for symmetry with the other
# *_VERSION keys.
KUBECTL_VERSION=v1.30.14

# ── Docker client toolchain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Client binaries only: the `docker` CLI plus the buildx and compose plugins, so
# a workspace can drive a Docker daemon. The daemon is NOT installed here — it is
# the per-workspace docker:29.8.1-dind sidecar that templates/docker-dev
# provisions, so this image must never gain dockerd, containerd, runc or
# docker-proxy (the static CLI tarball ships all of them, which is why the
# Dockerfile extracts the docker/docker member alone). DOCKER_HOST is
# deliberately not baked into ENV either: a baked endpoint would break the
# host-socket case, and the sidecar is wired from Terraform instead.
# All three asset URLs VERIFIED (HTTP 200) on 2026-09-28. DOCKER_CLI_VERSION is
# the same 29.8.1 engine line as that dind tag, so bump the two together.
# The upstream arch spellings differ, so the Dockerfile derives both spellings
# from TARGETARCH: download.docker.com and compose use x86_64/aarch64, buildx
# uses amd64/arm64.
DOCKER_CLI_VERSION=29.8.1
BUILDX_VERSION=v0.37.1
COMPOSE_VERSION=v5.5.1

# ── UNVERIFIED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No entries are currently unverified. Anything added here must state what could
# not be confirmed and why the build should still proceed.
